@startuml Events Query Flow - Clubinho NIB API
!theme plain
hide footbox

title Events — date-scoped queries

actor "Frontend" as client
participant EventController as controller
participant GetEventService as service
database "MySQL\nEvent + media repositories" as db
participant ClubMeetingScheduleService as schedule
participant "AWS S3" as s3

client -> controller : GET /events?from&to or /events/upcoming?from&to
controller -> controller : resolve public/private visibility
controller -> service : findAll or findUpcoming(range)
service -> db : load visible events + media metadata
db --> service : events ordered by date
service -> schedule : occurrencesByEvent(events, effective range)
schedule -> schedule : apply academic periods and exceptions
service --> client : 200 EventResponseDto[]
client -> s3 : load media from returned URLs

note over client, controller
  Cards: week/month send from + to; all omits both.
  Calendar: each visible month sends its first and last day.
end note

note over service, schedule
  /upcoming clamps from to today in the app timezone.
  Regular event: stored date within range.
  Club meeting: weekday within academic periods and range,
  excluding exceptions and dates before the series start.
  Events without occurrences are omitted.
end note

@enduml
